  "body": "Part of #894.\n\nThe `Thread` operation cuts only the 60-degree ISO metric / unified form: `camcraft_tools::thread_mill::form_refusal` refuses a thread mill ground to any other angle by name, and the depth is the ISO 724 constant `0.5413 x pitch`.\n\n**What is missing**\n- 55-degree Whitworth (BSW / BSP parallel): its own depth law (0.6403 x pitch, rounded crests and roots).\n- Taper pipe threads (NPT, BSPT): a ride whose radius changes with Z (a conical helix in short arcs), plus the taper mill form.\n- Trapezoidal and ACME forms (30 / 29 degrees).\n- Pitch entry in threads per inch for unified threads.\n\nEach form needs its depth law from the public standard (BS 84, ASME B1.20.1, ISO 2904, ASME B1.5), the form door widened to it, and the root / crest gouge readings (`operation::thread_op`) taking that depth.\n\n**Done means:** a thread mill of each supported form threads a modelled hole of that standard, verifies clean and posts; a form with no depth law is still refused by name; pinned by goldens.\n",
